{
  "alert_id" : "ALR-00002",
  "priority" : 1,
  "justification" : "TX-00454 brought 48000.00 CAD into C1059 from EXT-2224 by wire on 2026-09-16, and TX-00496 sent 45500.00 CAD (94.8% of it) out to EXT-2137 by wire about 5 hours later on the same day. Only 2500.00 CAD was retained, and the account has no other activity. This is a classic pass-through pattern, so the alert is raised to high priority."
}

{
  "case_id" : "CAS-00002",
  "description" : "Establish the source and purpose of the 48000.00 CAD wire TX-00454 from EXT-2224 and the reason for the 45500.00 CAD wire TX-00496 to EXT-2137 on 2026-09-16. Obtain the customer's explanation and supporting documents, such as an invoice or loan agreement. Confirm the identity of the EXT-2224 and EXT-2137 counterparties if the bank has any information on them.",
  "justification" : "C1059 has only two transactions. Funds were received and almost entirely forwarded within about 5 hours (TX-00454 on 2026-09-16 at 10:00 UTC, TX-00496 at 15:13 UTC), with 2500.00 CAD retained. No legitimate business explanation is visible in the data, so the source and purpose need to be established."
}

{
  "case_id" : "CAS-00002",
  "justification" : "C1059 received TX-00454, a 48000.00 CAD wire from EXT-2224 on 2026-09-16, and sent TX-00496, a 45500.00 CAD wire to EXT-2137 on the same day, about 5 hours 13 minutes later. That is 94.8% of the inflow passed on, and 2500.00 CAD was retained. The account has no other transactions, so it has no visible business activity that would explain a large wire being passed straight through. This matches the layering pattern of rapid pass-through, and the bank has no information that supports a legitimate purpose. Recommend the source and purpose of the funds be established before any decision on reporting. Note that the account profile and customer explanation were not available to this investigation."
}
